decision 2
  question "Which output columns does it produce, and how is each one computed (type, nullable) - e.g. amount_eur double not null = amount * rate?"
  answer "The schema columns, unchanged"
  by architect@example.com
  on 2026-11-11T19:06:57.730649+00:00

decision 3
  question "Does it group rows? By which keys, with which aggregates - e.g. by customer_id, sum(amount) as total - or no grouping?"
  answer "No grouping"
  by architect@example.com
  on 2026-11-11T19:06:57.982258+00:00

decision 4
  question "Does it join another dataset? Which one, on which keys, which join type, what if a key has no match - e.g. customers on customer_id, left join, no match keeps the row with empty customer columns - or no join? (a join needs a second input: archvow component edit <component> --signature \"(left: DataFrame, right: DataFrame) -> DataFrame\")"
  answer "No join"
  by architect@example.com
  on 2026-11-11T19:06:58.218911+00:00

decision 5
  question "Empty input (e.g. no orders on a holiday): return an empty DataFrame with the output schema, or fail?"
  answer "Return an empty DataFrame with the output schema"
  by architect@example.com
  on 2026-11-11T19:06:58.450589+00:00

decision 6
  question "Empty (null) values in the columns that identify a row (e.g. id is null): drop the row, keep it, or stop the job?"
  answer "Drop rows with a null order_id"
  by architect@example.com
  on 2026-11-11T19:06:58.685578+00:00

decision 7
  question "Duplicate keys in the input (e.g. two rows with id 42): keep first, keep last, aggregate, or fail?"
  answer "Keep one row per order_id"
  by architect@example.com
  on 2026-11-11T19:06:58.910478+00:00

decision 8
  question "Negative or out-of-range values (e.g. amount = -5): keep them, replace them by the nearest limit, drop the row, or stop the job?"
  answer "Drop rows where amount is negative"
  by architect@example.com
  on 2026-11-11T19:06:59.145793+00:00

decision 9
  question "Extra input columns not in the schema (e.g. a column added upstream): drop silently or fail?"
  answer "Drop them: output only the schema columns"
  by architect@example.com
  on 2026-11-11T19:06:59.389243+00:00

